From 432e9d609f0dfe5cb893c13f686466db291fd465 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:33:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] ASoC: ak4961: speaker playback over SLIMbus to the
 TFA9890 amplifiers

Stage 2 of the AK4961 port:
- init state of ZTE's driver, written after enumeration: the 44 registers
  that differ from reset in an idle register dump of the LineageOS 4.4
  port (PORT2/4 I2S masters from PLL1, PLL1 from the 9.6 MHz MCLK, ...)
- AIF1 playback DAI (ak4961_rx1) on PGD ports 10/11, SLIMbus stream
  prepare/enable per trigger, channel map from the machine driver
- PLL CLK supply (PMPLL, then PMAIF; off in reverse with DSPRSTN), the
  per-rate clock dividers of ZTE's hw_params, SB1 in the SLIMbus sync
  domain
- controls PORT2 Sync Domain and SDTO2 Source Selector (ZTE's speaker
  path: slimbus, SBI1)

DT: two TFA9890 on BLSP1 QUP6 (0x34/0x35, mainline tfa989x, resets on
PMI8994 GPIO 2/3 at 1.8 V) and a SLIMBUS_0_RX link with the AK4961 and
both amplifiers.

Tested: during playback the AK4961 registers equal the LineageOS dump
while it plays to the speaker, and both TFA9890 report PLL lock on the
AK4961's I2S clock, amplifier switching and power on (status 0xd85f,
idle 0x0a5d with NOCLK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FVN6i64chehV1XxwjxyaGp
